1
00:00:00,250 --> 00:00:03,800
Adherence OS is an AI decision layer for at-home GLP-1 care.

2
00:00:03,800 --> 00:00:15,400
It predicts next week's adherence interruption, explains the active driver, compares one bounded support route, and uses independent deterministic rules to decide when AI must stop and a clinician must review.

3
00:00:16,321 --> 00:00:23,000
Maya begins in coaching mode. Her synthetic eight-week history and today's check-in produce a five per cent next-week adherence-interruption estimate.

4
00:00:23,000 --> 00:00:27,200
Recent adherence is one hundred per cent.

5
00:00:27,200 --> 00:00:34,600
The evidence map surfaces appetite and energy drag, while the decision summary keeps one safe next move, a hydration nudge, visible beside the graph.

6
00:00:35,527 --> 00:00:40,200
Switching to Attribution shows where each part of the route comes from.

7
00:00:40,200 --> 00:00:45,200
Routine disruption accounts for thirty-two per cent of absolute local attribution.

8
00:00:45,200 --> 00:00:51,900
Blue nodes represent model evidence, amber nodes are bounded simulations, red nodes are deterministic rules, and grey-green nodes are patient context.

9
00:00:52,897 --> 00:00:56,500
Selecting Hydration nudge does not claim a treatment effect.

10
00:00:56,500 --> 00:01:03,400
The app changes explicit feature assumptions, rescores the same monotonic model, and shows a two percentage-point scenario decrease.

11
00:01:03,400 --> 00:01:09,500
It ranks the route only while both the observed and simulated vectors remain inside the synthetic training-support envelope.

12
00:01:10,429 --> 00:01:16,800
In Escalation, Maya reports severe abdominal pain, vomiting, poor hydration, and lightheadedness.

13
00:01:16,800 --> 00:01:24,200
The input moves outside synthetic support, so numeric model ranking abstains and every coaching route is suppressed.

14
00:01:24,200 --> 00:01:29,900
Deterministic safety remains active, selects a cautious NHS 111 route, and prepares an urgent handoff draft.

15
00:01:30,866 --> 00:01:35,500
The care queue opens on the selected review task.

16
00:01:35,500 --> 00:01:40,100
It shows the trigger, an unassigned owner, and the explicit state: draft only, not sent.

17
00:01:40,100 --> 00:01:46,800
Eight weeks of context, current red flags, the patient-facing draft, and the five-step audit trail are compressed for human review.

18
00:01:46,800 --> 00:01:49,900
Nothing is diagnosed, assigned, or delivered automatically.

19
00:01:50,868 --> 00:01:56,000
The patient workspace keeps input lightweight: a planned weekly dose, four symptom and wellbeing scores, mood, and short notes.

20
00:01:56,000 --> 00:02:02,300
The deterministic plan updates immediately, then exposes a seven-day support plan and longitudinal context.

21
00:02:02,300 --> 00:02:09,900
Field edits invalidate older in-flight requests so stale provider work cannot overwrite the visible decision.

22
00:02:10,895 --> 00:02:14,500
Model evidence is inspectable, not hidden behind a chatbot.

23
00:02:14,500 --> 00:02:19,000
The prospective target predicts the following week's planned adherence event.

24
00:02:19,000 --> 00:02:23,000
Patients are isolated across train, validation, and test.

25
00:02:23,000 --> 00:02:32,300
The browser loads a fourteen-feature logistic artifact with sixteen bootstrap members, exact log-odds decomposition, reliability bins, sensitivity checks, and support-aware abstention.

26
00:02:32,300 --> 00:02:36,900
All metrics are synthetic pipeline evidence, not clinical validation.

27
00:02:38,077 --> 00:02:41,800
This is why Adherence OS fits eMed.

28
00:02:41,800 --> 00:02:45,700
Patient impact comes from one clear action before dropout.

29
00:02:45,700 --> 00:02:49,600
Innovation comes from dual-track machine learning and safety.

30
00:02:49,600 --> 00:02:54,400
Feasibility comes from local inference, typed data, keyless fallback, and asynchronous review.

31
00:02:54,400 --> 00:02:58,700
The live story is simple: predict the interruption, explain the driver, and hand off before harm.
